 "title": "Proteasome Complex and Protein Expression Study",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the study of the proteasome complex and its role in protein expression. The 26S proteasome is involved in activating the UPR (Unfolded Protein Response) and degrading SEC12. The proteasome complex is composed of various subunits, including 20S core peptidase, Rpn1, Rpn2, Rpt2, and Rpt3. Researchers, including Martin Andreas and Restrepo Santiago Yori, have employed site-specific photocrosslinking to study the proteasome's structure and function. The study also involves the use of Bpa-containing base subcomplexes and E. coli BL21(DE3) for protein expression and purification.",
